{# IN·05 — incidents by the zone they fall in.

   Zones are presence-driven and do not overlap, so an incident falls in exactly
   one and the counts add up to the window. A point in NO zone is a row of its own
   ("unzoned") rather than a dropped record: an organization that has drawn no
   zones at all is the normal state.

   THE DRAWING IS THE ATLAS'S. A window nobody filed in has no axis, and the
   component says so in the house's own words — so this partial carries no empty
   state of its own. #}
<div class="c" data-w="zones">
    {{ atlas_chart(
        dashboard.zoneChart,
        'Incidents by zone',
        'Zones are presence-driven and do not overlap, so an incident falls in exactly one — the counts add up to the window.'
    ) }}
</div>
